 @{title='Living Ornament batch 1: shape language and first visual';kind='feature';body='F01-F06, initial F15/F16. Expand Organic Regions with stable region contract, mixed lobes/corridors, deep bays, thin necks, localized contour complexity, nesting and fitted boundaries. Expand Organic Boundary Ink with bold/colored double edges; Composition Phrasing and Animated Watercolor with anchors, quiet areas and shape-aware washes. Create separate Living Ornament scene with grouped controls. Parallel lanes: geometry, ink, composition/color after minimal contract agreement. Actual flat-color/outline visual must show substantially different shape families, calm and intricate contour stretches and legible large composition. Artistically inspect and iterate before adding pattern detail. Preserve existing Library behavior. One integrated review, publish compatible component updates, save, commit and merge.'},
 @{title='Living Ornament batch 2: complete pattern vocabulary';kind='feature';body='F07-F12. New Spiral Fill, Packed Circles & Rings, Membrane/Petal Divisions, Nested Contours and Decorated Ribbons; expand Region Hatching. Parallel lanes: spirals/circles; membranes/contours; hatching/ribbons. Stable per-region variation, fitted spacing, light/dark reversals and per-family controls. Demonstrate narrow/concave/large regions at multiple scales in one scene. Spirals pack varied sizes; circles retain gaps; membrane hubs form unequal curved petals; contours respect necks; ribbons support beads/stripes/ladder cells. Review actual composition and detail together, fix artistic/clipping issues, publish independent Library parts as one batch, save, commit and merge.'},
 @{title='Living Ornament batch 3: artistic orchestration and motion';kind='feature';body='F13-F20 completing F15/F16. Expand Region Styles & Split Transitions for stable motif assignment, quiet regions and neighbor-aware contrast; Organic Regions for coherent deformation; every pattern for attached/flowing/growing modes; Decorated Ribbons for growth and spacing; Composition Phrasing and Animated Watercolor for delayed local tension/release and migrating warmth. Parallel lanes: shape motion, pattern/ribbon motion, art direction/color. Integrate finished animated Living Ornament. Inspect sustained motion and paused full/detail frames: persistent identity, no accidental texture sliding/reseeding, deliberate density/rest, no uniform pulsing, readable warm/cool anchors. Iterate artistic defects. One batch review, Library updates, scene save/reopen, commit and merge.'},
 @{title='Living Ornament batch 4: structural transformations and polish';kind='feature';body='F21. Expand Organic Regions with occasional neck closure, region division and island creation; expand Region Styles & Split Transitions with parent/child identity and gradual daughter color/motif inheritance. Parallel geometry and style lanes after event contract agreement; independent regression/performance checks. Preserve uneven patches and deliberate timing, avoid popping or continuously unstable topology. Inspect events before/during/after and sustained animation, iterate visual/artistic defects. Demonstrate complete final scene, controls, save/reopen and invalid-edit retention. Publish reusable updates, independent batch review, commit and merge. Preserve original painting and saved values.'}
